{"id":"n-20261025-k1ukwv","category":"sports","display_title":"Tottenham Defeats Chelsea After Palmer Red Card","display_title_he":"טוטנהאם מנצחת את צ'לסי לאחר כרטיס אדום לפאלמר","short_summary":"Tottenham secured a rare away victory against Chelsea following an own goal by debutant goalkeeper Mike Penders and a late red card for Cole Palmer.","english_level":"C1","words":423,"reading_time":3,"image":null,"sources":[{"name":"BBC Sport","domain":"bbc.co.uk","url":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/articles/cqwy7x6e672eo","title":"Penders error & Palmer sees red - player ratings for Chelsea v Spurs","published_at":"2026-10-24T18:26:29.000Z"},{"name":"The Guardian","domain":"theguardian.com","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/24/xabia-alonso-urges-cole-palmer-to-learn-from-red-card-in-chelseas-defeat-to-tottenham","title":"Alonso urges Cole Palmer ‘to learn’ from red card in Chelsea’s defeat to Spurs","published_at":"2026-10-24T20:19:17.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-24T18:26:29.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-25T06:12:33.732Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":8,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["In a dramatic Premier League encounter at Stamford Bridge, Tottenham claimed a rare and historic victory against Chelsea, winning 2-0. The result was shaped by a combination of unfortunate defensive errors and severe disciplinary issues, leaving Chelsea manager Xabi Alonso to address a steep learning curve for his squad. Spurs managed to secure their triumph at Stamford Bridge for only the second time across forty-two visits, leaving manager Roberto De Zerbi hoping the team can use the success as a springboard for future weeks.","The match took a disastrous turn for Chelsea's young goalkeeper, Mike Penders. Making his first Premier League start in place of the injured Emiliano Martinez, the twenty-one-year-old endured a difficult night when he calamitously punched a corner kick from Mateus Fernandes into his own net under pressure from Jan-Paul van Hecke. Penders later let in a strike at his near post from Mathys Tel. Despite the heavy blunder, Alonso defended his goalkeeper publicly after the final whistle, emphasizing that the team wins and loses together and offering full support to the young player.","Compounding Chelsea's woes, playmaker Cole Palmer received a red card in the final stretch of the game after enduring nine minutes of ill-discipline. Having already been booked for causing a flashpoint by pushing over Fernandes, Palmer was dismissed following a late tackle on substitute Conor Gallagher. The flashpoint capped off a frustrating afternoon for the hosts, who also sorely missed the services of forward João Pedro due to an unspecified training injury.","Speaking to the media after the match, Alonso acknowledged that Palmer must harness greater maturity to navigate high-pressure moments. Although noting that the disciplinary lapse was not a broader character concern, especially after nearly being sent off against Everton previously, the manager stressed that the incident must serve as a crucial lesson for the future. Chelsea struggled to find a decisive moment in the final third, with players like Pedro Neto, Moises Caicedo, and Josh Acheampong putting in strong shifts but failing to prevent the defeat.","With Chelsea chasing the game and eventually reduced to ten men, Tottenham capitalized on their numerical advantage. In the eighty-seventh minute, winger Mathys Tel sealed the contest with a spectacular individual dribble and finish, scoring his first Premier League goal of the season. For Tottenham, who had previously won only once in thirty-four trips to west London, the triumph offers De Zerbi a strong platform to build upon as his side seeks consistent improvement game by game and week by week, having suffered enough in the past."],"facts":[{"fact":"Tottenham defeated Chelsea 2-0 at Stamford Bridge on October 24, 2026, marking only their second victory there in 42 visits.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Chelsea goalkeeper Mike Penders scored an own goal on his first Premier League start by punching a corner into his own net.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Mathys Tel sealed Tottenham's victory with an 87th-minute goal.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Chelsea playmaker Cole Palmer was sent off after receiving two yellow cards for challenges on Mateus Fernandes and Conor Gallagher.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Chelsea manager Xabi Alonso urged Palmer to show more maturity and learn from the red card incident.","sources":[2]}],"glossary":[{"text":"dramatic","lemma":"dramatic","pos":"adjective","he":"דרמטי","name":false},{"text":"Premier League","lemma":"Premier League","pos":"noun","he":"פרמייר ליג","name":true},{"text":"encounter","lemma":"encounter","pos":"noun","he":"מפגש","name":false},{"text":"Stamford Bridge","lemma":"Stamford Bridge","pos":"noun","he":"סטמפורד ברידג'","name":true},{"text":"Tottenham","lemma":"Tottenham","pos":"noun","he":"טוטנהאם","name":true},{"text":"claimed","lemma":"claim","pos":"verb","he":"השיג","name":false},{"text":"rare","lemma":"rare","pos":"adjective","he":"נדיר","name":false},{"text":"historic","lemma":"historic","pos":"adjective","he":"היסטורי","name":false},{"text":"victory","lemma":"victory","pos":"noun","he":"ניצחון","name":false},{"text":"Chelsea","lemma":"Chelsea","pos":"noun","he":"צ'לסי","name":true},{"text":"winning","lemma":"win","pos":"verb","he":"מנצח","name":false},{"text":"result","lemma":"result","pos":"noun","he":"תוצאה","name":false},{"text":"shaped","lemma":"shape","pos":"verb","he":"עוצב","name":false},{"text":"combination","lemma":"combination","pos":"noun","he":"שילוב","name":false},{"text":"unfortunate","lemma":"unfortunate","pos":"adjective","he":"מצער","name":false},{"text":"defensive","lemma":"defensive","pos":"adjective","he":"הגנתי","name":false},{"text":"errors","lemma":"error","pos":"noun","he":"טעויות","name":false},{"text":"severe","lemma":"severe","pos":"adjec